 "scope": [
  "compared with X_ITE 16.6.0 in scene mode: sensors in a Transform with a Shape sibling (X_ITE 16.6.0 does not traverse a group that holds only a pick sensor, so the fixtures add a 0.02 unit Box beside each sensor); BOUNDS and GEOMETRY (Sphere against Box where the boxes overlap and the geometries do not), sortOrder CLOSEST / ANY / ALL / ALL_SORTED, objectType filter, pickable false, enabled false",
  "a shape outside every PickableGroup is not pickable here (as 19775-1 asks); X_ITE 16.6.0 picks it, the fixture checks it in ours only",
  "disabling a sensor that is active raises isActive false here; X_ITE 16.6.0 keeps it true, checked in ours only",
  "a Sphere picking geometry is a 162 point hull (0.4 percent inside the true sphere); the target is the convex hull of its mesh, so a concave target counts as its hull, as in X_ITE 16.6.0",
  "the hull of the pickingGeometry is made when first needed and cached by geometry node, so a pickingGeometry node that is replaced is picked up on the next timestamp; non-uniform scale on the sensor is applied to the hull"
